{"book":{"id":"book-the-comeback-how-aboriginals-are-reclaiming-power-and-influence-john-ralston-saul","slug":"the-comeback-how-aboriginals-are-reclaiming-power-and-influence-john-ralston-saul","title":"The Comeback: How Aboriginals Are Reclaiming Power and Influence","authors":[{"id":"person-john-ralston-saul","name":"John Ralston Saul"}],"isbn13":["9780670068739"],"subjects":["Race & Ethnicity"],"topics":["Media, Journalism & Public Opinion","Social Movements & Activism","Law & Legal Change","American Politics"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=The%20Comeback%3A%20How%20Aboriginals%20Are%20Reclaiming%20Power%20and%20Influence%20John%20Ralston%20Saul","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=The%20Comeback%3A%20How%20Aboriginals%20Are%20Reclaiming%20Power%20and%20Influence%20John%20Ralston%20Saul","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=The%20Comeback%3A%20How%20Aboriginals%20Are%20Reclaiming%20Power%20and%20Influence%20John%20Ralston%20Saul","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=The%20Comeback%3A%20How%20Aboriginals%20Are%20Reclaiming%20Power%20and%20Influence%20John%20Ralston%20Saul","publisher":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24347560W"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-shaughnessy-cohen-political-writing-wikipedia-shaughnessy-cohen-prize-for-political-writing","source-open-library-the-comeback-how-aboriginals-are-reclaiming-power-and-influence-john-ralston-saul","source-open-library-summary-the-comeback-how-aboriginals-are-reclaiming-power-and-influence-john-ralston-saul"],"publicationYear":2014,"thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10871734-L.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0,"accessibilityScore":0,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"renownProfile":{"knowsBook":true,"publicFame":42,"criticalRenown":55,"controversy":48,"llmAffinity":82,"affinityResidual":4.49,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.86,"criticalRenown":0.8,"controversy":0.75,"llmAffinity":0.9},"tags":{"craft":"craft-of-explanation","evidence":"synthesis-of-scholarship","stance":"revisionism"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"summary":"Once again, John Ralston Saul presents the story of Canada's past so that we may better understand its present -- and imagine a better future. Historic moments are always uncomfortable, Saul writes in this impassioned argument, calling on all of us to embrace and support the comeback of Aboriginal peoples. This, he says, is the great issue of our time -- the most important missing piece in the building of Canada. The events that began late in 2012 with the Idle No More movement were not just a rough patch in Aboriginal relations with the rest of Canada. What is happening today between Aboriginals and non-Aboriginals is not about guilt or sympathy or failure or romanticization of the past. It is about citizens' rights. It is about rebuilding relationships that were central to the creation of Canada. These relationships are just as important to its continued existence. The centrality of Aboriginal issues and peoples has the potential to open up a more creative way of imagining ourselves and a more honest narrative for Canada. Wide in scope but piercing in detail, The Comeback presents a powerful portrait of modern Aboriginal life in Canada, in contrast with the perceived failings so often portrayed in politics and in media.","subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Indigenous peoples","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-comeback-how-aboriginals-are-reclaiming-power-and-influence-john-ralston-saul"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Social conditions","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-comeback-how-aboriginals-are-reclaiming-power-and-influence-john-ralston-saul"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Indigenous peoples, canada","sourceId":"source-o